        "cap": "A boy has just thrown a ball, which flies toward a leaping dog."
      },
      {
        "t": "key",
        "html": "<b>ject</b> = <b>throw</b>. <b>mit</b>, <b>miss</b> = <b>send, let go</b>."
      },
      {
        "t": "p",
        "html": "A prefix tells you where the throwing or sending goes. <b>dejected</b>: thrown down. <b>interject</b>: thrown in between. <b>conjecture</b>: thrown together (a guess put together from scraps). <b>intermittent</b>: letting go in between, so stopping and starting. <b>remiss</b>: let go back, slack."
      },
      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "The parts and their words"
      },
      {
        "t": "viz",
        "name": "vo-roots",
        "opts": {
          "max": 10,
          "roots": [
            "ject",
            "mit"
          ]
        },
        "cap": "Words on the list built on ject and mit."
      },
      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "Words taken apart"
      },
      {
        "t": "table",
        "head": [
          "Word and meaning",
          "Parts, and what they say"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "<b>conjecture</b><br>a guess made without full evidence",
            "con- <i>together</i> + <b>ject</b> <i>throw</i> + -ure<br>→ “a throwing together (of guesses)”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>dejected</b><br>sad and discouraged",
            "de- <i>down</i> + <b>ject</b> <i>throw</i> + -ed<br>→ “thrown down”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>interject</b><br>to break in with a remark",
            "inter- <i>between</i> + <b>ject</b> <i>throw</i><br>→ “throw in between”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>intermittent</b><br>stopping and starting",
            "inter- <i>between</i> + <b>mitt</b> <i>let go</i> + -ent<br>→ “letting go in between”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>remiss</b><br>careless about one’s duties",
            "re- <i>back</i> + <b>miss</b> <i>let go</i><br>→ “let go slack”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>submit</b><br>to give in to authority",
            "sub- <i>under</i> + <b>mit</b> <i>send</i><br>→ “send under (give in)”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>premise</b><br>a statement assumed true and used to reason toward a conclusion",
            "pre- <i>before</i> + <b>mis</b> <i>send</i> + -e<br>→ “a thing sent before”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>demise</b><br>death, or the end of something",
            "de- <i>away</i> + <b>mis</b> <i>send</i> + -e<br>→ “a sending away (an end)”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>unremitting</b><br>never relaxing or slackening",
            "un- <i>not</i> + re- <i>back</i> + <b>mitt</b> <i>let go</i> + -ing<br>→ “never letting up”"
          ]
        ],
        "cap": "Each word, what it means now, and its parts."
      },
      {
        "t": "ex",
        "title": "Use the parts",
        "q": "The movie <b>projector</b> threw a bright picture onto the wall. Explain the word.",
        "steps": [
          "Take it apart: <b>pro-</b> (forward) + <b>ject</b> (throw) + <b>-or</b> (a thing that).",
          "Literally: “a thing that throws forward.”",
          "A projector throws light forward onto a screen."
        ],
        "a": "A machine that throws a picture forward onto a screen."
      },
